<title>ITALY: Milan airports air cargo traffic up 3.1pct.</title>
<headline>Milan airports air cargo traffic up 3.1pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo traffic handled by Milan's airport system increased 3.1 percent to 14,114 tonnes in February 1997 against the same period 1996, the operating company SEA said.</p>
<p>This was despite the bad weather conditions in the first two months of the year and demonstrations by farmers, which had a negative effect on Linate operations, it added.</p>
<p>		    Total Milan system</p>
